      <Docs>
        <param name="packageIdentifier">The PackageIdentifier used as the target package in a call to PackageManager.canPackageQuery(String, String) to determine whether a caller satisfies the public-visibility condition. This value may be null.</param>
        <summary>Sets the target package for the public-visibility condition.</summary>
        <returns>This builder instance.</returns>
        <remarks>
          <para>Sets the target package for the public-visibility condition, which is checked with PackageManager.canPackageQuery(String, String). The target can differ from the package performing the indexing, for example when an on-device indexer processes information about other packages. The check uses the target package regardless of which package indexed the document. Other visibility requirements may also apply. Passing null removes this public-visibility condition from the configuration.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/appsearch/SchemaVisibilityConfig.Builder#setPubliclyVisibleTargetPackage(android.app.appsearch.PackageIdentifier)" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.app.appsearch.SchemaVisibilityConfig.Builder.setPubliclyVisibleTargetPackage</code>.</a></format></para>
